/**
 * Reference matrices from an independent, widely-deployed QR implementation.
 *
 * WHY FIXTURES AND NOT PROPERTIES: a QR encoder with a wrong format bit or a
 * mis-shifted BCH generator still produces a tidy, plausible square — it simply
 * decodes to nothing. Structural assertions (right size, finders in place) pass
 * happily on such a thing. Only comparing against a matrix known to scan catches
 * it, which is exactly how the two bugs in the first draft of lib/qr.ts were
 * found: the format bits were written LSB-first instead of MSB-first, and the
 * version-information BCH loop ran twelve times instead of six.
 *
 * The cases are chosen to straddle every boundary in the spec that changes the
 * output: v1 (no alignment pattern), v4-6 (alignment, no version block), v6+
 * (both), and v10 (where the byte-mode character count widens from 8 bits to
 * 16). All four error-correction levels appear.
 */
